+<h2><!--n-->. The no-allowance warning's edge whitespace and lone backslash are pinned: cells O5 and O6 in the KS-1480 suite (KS-1504)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> Tests only. <code>Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1480-no-allowance-warning-fields-are-escaped.test.ts</code> gains two cells in its <code>O</code> group, items 3 and 4 of KS-1504 (the KS-1496 gate's notes n2 and n3). <strong>O5:</strong> a leading or trailing space in a principal or a tenant is written to the warning as typed (four variants, each with its own tenant so no two share a throttle slot), with controls that the trimmed fragment is absent. <strong>O6:</strong> a lone backslash is written as two (in a principal, and at the end of a tenant), and two typed backslashes as four, read by a helper that is itself checked against one, two and no backslash. The completeness count <code>EXPECTED_CELLS</code> moves from 13 to 15.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>What does not change:</strong> <code>src/middleware/rateLimitEnforce.ts</code> is untouched (blob <code>cc5a35e68114</code>, equal to develop's), so there is no deploy surface. Item 1 of the ticket (the product change, <code>logField(user.authMethod)</code>) landed earlier in PR 1584. <strong>Not built:</strong> item 2, exporting a frozen set or a predicate so a test can read runtime membership; the ticket marks it optional.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Why these two.</strong> Before this change no cell had a leading or trailing space in a principal or tenant, so a final <code>.trim()</code> on <code>logField</code> (gate mutant X5) or a trim before the JSON step (E1) stayed green and silently dropped a trailing space from an id. P3 pins the double quote and the typed-versus-real difference, not the backslash on its own, so leaving the backslash single while the quote stayed escaped (Q4) kept P3 green.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>Each cell is green on the product and red under its own mutant; the old suite does not see X5 or E1.</strong></td><td> <strong>Mutants applied to the product file in a scratch clone, restored to develop's blob after each run (the script prints the hash check):</strong> X5 gives O5 red and the old ks1480 suite 14 of 14 green; E1 the same; Q4 gives O6 red and O3 red, and the old suite red only on O3 (the indirect catch the ticket names). P3 stays green under Q4, as the ticket says. The unmutated run is 16 of 16 (new file), 14 of 14 (old file), 6 of 6 (ks1504 file).
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Whole suite:</strong> api-gateway before <strong>1623 passed, 0 failed</strong> (154 files); after <strong>1625 passed, 0 failed</strong> (154 files): +2 cells, +0 files. The test-type ratchet (leg 16) for api-gateway reads 25 errors, all 25 in the baseline, 0 new, 0 stale, 154 test files examined. eslint on the changed file is clean, and a planted <code>debugger</code> statement makes the same command fail (control).
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Host and versions:</strong> an Apple Silicon (arm64) Mac, Darwin 27.0.0, shared with other seats; Node v26.8.1 (the repo's stated LTS line is 24, so these figures were NOT measured on Node 24); vitest 4.1.12. Not run: the four platform suites and the push hook's Docker legs.
+    </td></tr></table>
